course: dictionary
lesson: 6701
title: Octopus
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An octopus is a sea animal with a soft, round body and eight long arms covered in suckers. Its name comes from Greek, and «octo» means eight, just like in an octagon, the shape with eight sides.
explain: Context gives clues too. «A squid has 8 arms and 2 longer tentacles, and like an octopus it has 3 hearts.» The sentence compares the two animals, so you can see that the octopus also has eight arms and three hearts.
explain: «Other reef animals win by tricks: an octopus that pretends to be a lionfish and then a sea snake.» Pretends means acts like something else to fool others. Ask yourself what word would fit, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: An octopus is a mollusc, but it has no shell.
fact: Octopuses have three hearts and blue blood.
fact: «Camouflage» means hiding by changing colour or shape to look like the things around you, and octopuses are masters of it.
fact: «Octopus ink» is a dark liquid that an octopus squirts out to escape from danger.
fact: The usual English plural of octopus is octopuses.
exercise: «A squid has 8 arms and 2 longer tentacles, and like an octopus it has 3 hearts.» How many hearts does an octopus have? | *Three | One | Two | Eight
exercise: What does «octo» mean, as in octagon? | Ten | *Eight | Four | Six
exercise: An octopus changes its colour to hide from a fish. What is this called? | *Camouflage | Speed | A shell | Ink
test: What is an octopus? | A snake that lives in trees | A bird with a long beak | *A sea animal with a soft, round body and eight long arms | A fish with a spiky shell
test: What does an octopus squirt out to escape? | *Ink | Milk | Sand | Blood
exam: Which is the usual English plural of octopus? | Octopodes | Octopusses | Octopi | *Octopuses
